    "description": "Arrowhead Lot\nMixed Stone Projectile Points\n16 Items, Various Materials\nThis collection of sixteen projectile points features a diverse range of lithic materials and knapping styles. The lot includes various point shapes including corner-notched, side-notched, and stemmed bases, reflecting common regional designs. These pieces serve as excellent examples of stone tool craftsmanship across different mineral types such as obsidian, chert, and jasper. No brand name or maker's mark is readable on any of the items.\nITEMS INCLUDED:\n1.\nBlack Obsidian Point\n- Glassy volcanic stone, approximately 2.5 inches\n2.\nRed Jasper-style Point\n- Dark red stone with fine flaking\n3.\nGrey Chert Point\n- Speckled grey material, stemmed base\n4.\nTan Chert Point\n- Light tan stone, corner-notched\n5.\nBrown Flint Point\n- Deep brown stone, side-notched\n6.\nMottled Grey/Brown Point\n- Largest piece in lot, approximately 3.75 inches, stemmed base\n7.\nLight Grey Stone Point\n- Triangular shape, small size\n8.\nRed Ochre Point\n- Large, elongated reddish stone point\n9.\nDark Grey Stone Point\n- Side-notched with tapered tip\n10.\nBrick Red Point\n- Small, sturdy point with corner notches\n11.\nSpeckled Tan Point\n- Textured stone with tapered base\n12.\nDark Brown Point\n- Mottled flint-like material\n13.\nGrey/Tan Point\n- Leaf-shaped design\n14.\nSmall Red Point\n- Compact point, roughly knapped\n15.\nMedium Grey Point\n- Standard chert construction\n16.\nLight Tan Point\n- Smooth surface, triangular base\nCondition:\nGood vintage condition. All items show authentic weathering and percussion flaking marks. Most pieces show adhesive residue or tape remnants on the reverse side from previous display mounting. Several points exhibit minor edge chips consistent with age. All pieces appear structurally sound.",
